cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Geospatial modelling of pluvial flood scenarios and their
  effects on physical access to maternal and child healthcare
  facilities
message: >-
  If you use this software or dataset, please cite it using
  the metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Rik Ubbo
    family-names: Lubbers
    email: r.u.lubbers@rug.nl
    affiliation: University of Groningen / University Medical Center Groningen
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2772-1524'
abstract: >-
  Analytical codebase for a study examining how urban pluvial
  floods alter walking access to healthcare facilities in
  Kampala, Uganda. The pipeline estimates population-weighted
  changes in travel time under 15 rainfall × duration
  scenarios for public, private-not-for-profit, and hospital
  facilities. Inequities are quantified by intersecting flood
  impact with a composite vulnerability index derived from
  socio-economic and health indicators.
keywords:
  - pluvial flooding
  - healthcare accessibility
  - travel time modelling
  - AccessMod
  - Kampala
  - Uganda
  - vulnerability
  - maternal and child health
  - geospatial analysis
